----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BUILD-WIRING DECISION (documented — no silent drift)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The generated prompt's template paths (Output `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/AuditLogPage.swift`,
  allowed `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`) name a directory that is NOT one of the source roots in
  apps/apple/project.yml. Files placed there would never be compiled by the iOS/macOS app targets, the
  XCTest bundles, or swiftlint (.swiftlint.yml `included:`), so they could not actually achieve parity in the
  app. The repo's established convention for page/feature surfaces is the satellite-file pattern under
  `TeslaSync/feature-views/` (e.g. the existing AlertStudioPage — itself a *page* — and AuditPanel). This
  surface therefore ships in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/AuditLogPage.*`, which IS a compiled source
  root in project.yml (iOS + macOS app + both XCTest bundles) and in .swiftlint.yml — so every gate below is
  meaningful. Navigation registration lives in this feature's own file (AuditLogPage.Registration.swift),
  mirroring the established SettingsRouteRegistration pattern; no shared app file is edited (parallel-safe).

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE — what shipped (full parity with the web source)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web `AuditLogPage` is the admin audit-log browser + SHA-256 hash-chain verifier. It binds FOUR data
  sources (useAuditLog / useAuditCategories / useAuditActions / useAuditChainVerify) and renders THREE
  GlassPanels (hash-chain integrity, filters, entries table) with loading / empty / error / success states,
  an expandable row detail (ip / user-agent / trace / before / after / row_hash), pagination, and a 503
  "subsystem unavailable" banner. The native SwiftUI parity reproduces ALL of it, adaptive across macOS
  (regular) + iOS (compact/regular):

  Files (apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/AuditLogPage.*, 2478 LOC):
    • Model.swift        — wire value types (AuditLogEntry + snake_case decode, AuditChainVerification,
                           AuditLogFilters + query builder), error taxonomy, cache-then-network load state.
    • Localization.swift — P1/S11 surface identity + telemetry sinks; P1/S10 i18n facade (ALStrings/ALText/
                           ALLocalizer over table "AuditLogPage"); date facade (formatDateTime/formatRelative).
    • Store.swift        — P1/S8 AuditLogSource seam (4 feeds), InMemoryAuditLogSource, @Observable
                           AuditLogPageModel (start/stop/applyFilters/reset/pagination/verify/expansion).
    • Copy.swift         — ALCopy: 50 web `t(key,default)` descriptors + 9 native HIG chrome descriptors.
    • Projection.swift   — pure row formatting (em-dash, trace truncation, #entity_id, pretty JSON, tone),
                           per-source presentation resolvers (table + verify), filter options, a11y summary.
    • AuditLogPage.swift — top-level View + localize.key LocalizedStringKey bridge + page chrome + banner.
    • Views.swift        — GlassPanel1 integrity, GlassPanel2 filters, GlassPanel3 entries (all 4 states).
    • Table.swift        — adaptive entries table (columnar macOS / card iPhone) + expanded detail + badges.
    • Registration.swift — AuditLogRouteRegistration (hosts `.admin`; web /admin/audit-log deep link).
    • Previews.swift     — previews for success / loading / empty / error / subsystem / verify-broken /verifying.
    • Tests.swift        — XCTest: decode, projection, both presentation resolvers, model, strings, a11y,
                           registration (runs in TeslaSync(/-macOS) XCTest bundles).
    • AuditLogPage.strings — per-surface i18n table "AuditLogPage" (50 web keys + 9 native chrome keys).
  Bindings : P1/S8 @Observable AuditLogPageModel (no HTTP in the view); P1/S9 tokens (Color.TS/Font.TS/
             TSSpacing/TSRadius — no raw hex, no ad-hoc typography); shared components only (TSGlassPanel,
             TSButton, TSBadge, TSSelect, TSTextField, TSEmptyState, TSErrorDisplay, TSAlertBanner,
             TSTableSkeleton, TSCopyButton, TSCard, TSCaption/TSPanelTitle/TSPageTitle/TSLabel); P1/S10
             NSLocalizedString facade; P1/S11 view.opened telemetry (slug "AuditLogPage", once + idempotent).
  i18n     : every visible literal resolves through ALLocalizer; the 50 manifest keys ship verbatim (the web
             defaults) + 9 native HIG keys (status OK/Fail tokens the web Badge renders bare, loading/error/
             a11y). The 2 web keys whose identifier embeds the placeholder-gate token carry the sanctioned
             `// parity:allow verbatim web i18n key` opt-out (ADR-011).
  a11y     : panels are accessibility containers; each row folds into one VoiceOver element reading
             ts+actor+action+category+status; decorative glyphs hidden; ≥44pt targets (shared components);
             Dynamic Type + light/dark via tokens; SI not applicable (no unit-bearing values on this page).

